{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3","c4"],"primary":"c1","title":"Prohibition on the sale or use of coordinated pricing algorithms to set rents or manage occupancy levels (BMC Chapter 13.63)","requirement":"It is unlawful to sell, license or otherwise provide a coordinated pricing algorithm to Berkeley landlords, and unlawful for a landlord to use one, to set or recommend rents or occupancy levels for residential units in Berkeley. Each unit and each month of a violation is a separate violation, and both the City Attorney and aggrieved tenants may sue for injunctive relief, damages and civil penalties.","key_value":"Ban on selling or using coordinated pricing algorithms; civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; Competitor Data = non-public data less than 90 days old","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Municipal Code ch. 13.63; Ordinance No. 7,992-N.S.","coverage_conditions":"All residential dwelling units in the City of Berkeley. Applies to landlords and to anyone who sells or licenses such algorithms to Berkeley landlords.","exemptions":"The following are excluded from the definition of coordinated pricing algorithm: (a) products or processes that publish aggregated, anonymous rental data without recommending rents, fees, occupancy rates or terms; (b) products used to set rent or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing guidelines; (c) products or processes used for market research for project financing, appraisals, or research, testing or training for software development, provided Competitor Data is not an input when a recommendation is calculated for a Berkeley landlord.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
